<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <title>BTA FMS Customer Dashboard</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/styles.css" />
  </head>
  <body class="workspace-page">
    <main class="workspace-shell">
      <section class="hero-band">
        <div class="hero-copy">
          <p class="eyebrow">Customer Services</p>
          <h1>BTA Passenger Services Portal</h1>
          <p class="subtitle">
            Signed in as <strong><%= user.username %></strong>. Book tickets, inspect active buses,
            and check ticket state from the customer workspace while every action emits structured
            JSON logs for Graylog.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="hero-actions">
          <nav class="page-nav">
            <a class="nav-link active" href="/customer/dashboard">Customer Dashboard</a>
            <a class="nav-link" href="/customer/book-ticket">Book Ticket</a>
            <a class="nav-link" href="/customer/buses">Buses In Operation</a>
            <a class="nav-link" href="/customer/ticket-status">Ticket Status</a>
          </nav>
          <form method="post" action="/logout">
            <button class="secondary" type="submit">Log Out</button>
          </form>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="metric-grid">
        <article class="metric-card">
          <p class="metric-label">App Name</p>
          <p class="metric-value">bta-fms</p>
        </article>
        <article class="metric-card">
          <p class="metric-label">Role</p>
          <p class="metric-value">customer</p>
        </article>
        <article class="metric-card">
          <p class="metric-label">Graylog Search</p>
          <p class="metric-value">app_name:bta-fms</p>
        </article>
        <article class="metric-card">
          <p class="metric-label">Bus Updates</p>
          <p class="metric-value">Live JSON lookups</p>
        </article>
      </section>

      <section class="operation-grid">
        <article class="operation-card">
          <div class="card-topline">
            <p class="eyebrow">Booking</p>
            <span class="status-pill success">customer_ticket_booking</span>
          </div>
          <h2>Book Ticket</h2>
          <p>
            Fill in passenger, route, bus, seat, payment, and travel details. Submitting the form
            creates a new booking record and emits a dedicated booking log for Graylog. The same
            page can also trigger any admin-armed payment terminal scenario when the terminal ID
            matches.
          </p>
          <ul class="detail-list">
            <li>Pre-filled defaults mirror a realistic daily commute booking.</li>
            <li>The response shows the generated BTA ticket number immediately.</li>
            <li>Use the same terminal ID as the admin DNS or skimming profile to prove that path.</li>
          </ul>
          <a class="link-button" href="/customer/book-ticket">Open Booking Console</a>
        </article>

        <article class="operation-card">
          <div class="card-topline">
            <p class="eyebrow">Operations</p>
            <span class="status-pill neutral">customer_bus_lookup</span>
          </div>
          <h2>Current Buses</h2>
          <p>
            Search buses in operation by route, origin, destination, and vehicle status. The page
            returns live bus cards and logs the exact query fields you used. If an admin has armed a
            spoofing profile, the returned bus view will reflect the ghost-bus data.
          </p>
          <ul class="detail-list">
            <li>Useful for route discovery and current fleet visibility.</li>
            <li>Every lookup remains visible in Graylog with operator labels.</li>
            <li>Matching spoofed buses emit GPS anomaly logs on the same lookup.</li>
          </ul>
          <a class="link-button" href="/customer/buses">Open Bus Console</a>
        </article>

        <article class="operation-card">
          <div class="card-topline">
            <p class="eyebrow">Ticket Tracking</p>
            <span class="status-pill warn">customer_ticket_status_lookup</span>
          </div>
          <h2>Check Ticket Status</h2>
          <p>
            Search by ticket number, passenger, contact, bus, or status. The page returns matching
            tickets and emits a structured ticket-status lookup event for Graylog visibility.
          </p>
          <ul class="detail-list">
            <li>Supports broad searches or exact ticket lookups.</li>
            <li>Rendered results and raw JSON stay on-screen after each query.</li>
          </ul>
          <a class="link-button" href="/customer/ticket-status">Open Status Console</a>
        </article>
      </section>

      <section class="detail-layout">
        <article class="detail-card detail-card-wide">
          <div class="card-topline">
            <p class="eyebrow">Graylog Visibility</p>
            <span class="status-pill success">Quick Search Keys</span>
          </div>
          <h2>Customer Log Queries</h2>
          <div class="chip-wrap">
            <span class="data-chip">app_name:bta-fms</span>
            <span class="data-chip">message:customer_ticket_booking</span>
            <span class="data-chip">message:customer_bus_lookup</span>
            <span class="data-chip">message:customer_ticket_status_lookup</span>
            <span class="data-chip">message:payment_card_read_anomaly</span>
            <span class="data-chip">message:dns_tunneling_suspected</span>
            <span class="data-chip">message:gps_signal_anomaly</span>
            <span class="data-chip">message:http_access</span>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="detail-card">
          <div class="card-topline">
            <p class="eyebrow">How To Verify</p>
            <span class="status-pill neutral">Graylog</span>
          </div>
          <ul class="detail-list">
            <li>Run an action from one of the customer consoles.</li>
            <li>For hands-on admin scenarios, first arm the terminal or bus from the admin dashboard.</li>
            <li>Search `app_name:bta-fms` in Graylog with a recent time range.</li>
            <li>Add one of the message names above to isolate the event category.</li>
          </ul>
        </article>
      </section>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
